# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Do not commit .env.
# PUBLIC_URL is the HTTPS origin already configured for ngrok (or your domain).
# It is not a secret. Leave it blank to keep browser calls on the same host.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://your-subdomain.ngrok-free.app
# APP_URL is an alias of PUBLIC_URL. APP_BASE_URL is only the keep-alive ping.
# SERVER_MODE=private keeps anonymous internet clients off protected APIs.
# Set SERVER_MODE=public when the server should accept browsers that have not
# logged in yet (the login page itself is always reachable). A password + OTP
# login registers that device and returns a session token either way.
# SERVER_MODE=private
# SHARE_PUBLIC_KEY is the optional signup-page door. Never put it in the frontend.
# MASTER_KEY and SIGNING_SECRET stay in .env only.
